From 8f3def5bf2ec080340590e691f11135a0eff92a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Christian=20K=C3=BCndig?= <christian@kuendig.info>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:38:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] tests: Allow other drivers in every CUDA topology section

The section listener clears DXVK_NVAPI_ALLOW_OTHER_DRIVERS whenever a
section starts, so setting it once per test case did not admit the
mocked non-NVIDIA adapters and NvAPI_Initialize failed. Set it right
before initializing instead. Also apply clang-format to the CUDA test
helper, and keep the undocumented interface table in the SDK layout
that validate-methods.py expects.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/nvapi_interface_undocumented.h |  3 ++
 tests/nvapi_sysinfo_cuda.cpp       | 66 ++++++++++++++----------------
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

